rayjs for generated9

Rebuild and install /sys/src/cmd/6c first: the bootstrap lacks the comparison
and register-save fixes needed by QuickJS. Build libgpu, TinyGL and raylib
(boot/GPU.md), then:

    cd /sys/src/cmd/rayjs
    mk install
    games/gemrun
    games/gemrun -a

mk builds the native QuickJS core from ../quickjs/native as needed.
The existing APE qjs and qjsc remain independent. No host compiler is needed.

Scripts import the built-in raylib module. See rayjs(1) for the supported
API and lifetimes, and /sys/games/lib/gemrun for a complete game.

Tests in a rio window with VirGL:

    cd /sys/src/cmd/rayjs
    mk test
    ./6.out test/audio.js
    ./6.out /sys/games/lib/gemrun/main.js -n 120 -o /tmp/gemrun.png

Audio is optional and needs /dev/audio. Tests cover language and module
loading, numeric behavior, heap/stack limits, drawing state, resource lifetime,
argument getters, game rules, exceptions and rejected promises. The window
test writes /tmp/rayjs-pixels.png: green and red squares on a dark blue field,
a gold model, a magenta sphere and text. Runtime validation: amd64,
QEMU VirGL and HDA.

QuickJS and raylib versions and licenses are recorded in CREDITS.md and their
UPSTREAM files. rayjs, Gemrun and its mesh are generated9 contributions under
the root LICENSE.
